If you connect the mic to the front panel you will almost certainly get noise pickup. Not much I can do about that as it is due to the common ground with the processor. <br><br>It is OK for using the keypad though. <br><br>I did consider adding locating pins to the top of the front panel cover. But they would be tiny and probably not print anyway. <br><br>Regarding modifying the original plastic, I didn't do that. I tapped the screws into the new plastic and left them as locating pins which just went Into the holes on the original. The front panel was then held in place just by the bottom screws. <br><br><br>Colin.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Fri Sep 08, 2023 1:30 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
